Z||000005||AusFiero||07-24-2001||12:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BC-GT:<BR><B>Wow, thats a great deal, what brand are they?<BR>Australia is looking better and better in my books (except for all those huge poisonous reptiles and bugs)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I got a Kodak DC4800 with a bonus 32 meg card as well as the 16 meg card with it. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dc4800.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.kodak.com.au/US/en/digital/cameras/dc4800/" TARGET=_blank>Kodak Camera Specs Page</A><P>The video they gave me is a Hitachi VME 368OE<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hitachi368.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.hitachi.com.au/publishfiles/flashmenu/frame1.htm" TARGET=_blank>Hitachi Camera Specs Page</A><BR>Bear in mind our prices are different to yours and it is excellent value here I assure you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>LOL on the bugs and reptiles. ummmm we never see much around poisonous where I live. Ok we have spiders but they can't kill you. Well funnel webs can but with maybe 1 death a year from 19,000,000 people it isn't a big problem. Our reptiles are little pussycats except the snakes. But again you don't see many of them around even in the bush. Only have 2 deadly species and most people don't die even from their bites as it is a slow death. Lots of time to get to hospital and get fixed.<BR>Least we haven't got bears and stuff that can chase and eat. I think death by Australian predators and snakes and stuff is about 8 to 10 a year in total.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
